nodes.body:
@dhayanesh This requires `params.json` for object storage but not for local paths. The default loader never uses `params.json` as a detection signal. Why was this condition added only for object storage?
The local path to the metadata is caching metadata files which originated from the object storage path of the model. Therefore, the condition can be the same as in the default loader.

If a model has consolidated weights in S3 but the local config dir doesn't have `params.json` (e.g., model was loaded from HF Hub cache path), it silently loads all HF shards, breaking the same way the issue reports.

